Object class: Euclid

Special containment procedures: SCP-5181 must be kept in a 30 by 30cm box lined with strong synthetic padding.

The sealed box is then submerged in the center of the 10m polyethylene holding tank.

it should be sufficient to decrease the kinetic activity of SCP-5181 for adequate recovery by containment personnel.

All personnel entering the SCP-5181 containment chamber must wear specialized coating (found in Note SCP-5181)

and one and a breathing apparatus before being lowered into the polyethylene tank. and a breathing apparatus before being lowered into the polyethylene tank.

If SCP-5181 is loose outside the polyethylene tank, personnel are advised to protect themselves in a separate room and close the doors.

or hatches to isolate SCP-5181 until the arrival of the containment teams.

[quarter past eleven]

Description: SCP-5181 has the appearance of a  manufactured by the company OLM in 1997. It is six (6) centimeters in diameter and is red.

At first considered a pleasant and harmless child's toy, SCP-5181 was able to spin up to 3,000 times its normal speed, making it an authentic

metal tornado capable of reaching about 3,000 times its normal speed. CP-5181 was found by founding agents in the city of ███████ em ███████

after several reports from the population of a metal  it destroyed several houses and caused more than three deaths and several injured. According to reports by

SCP-5181 Foundation

it simply stopped spinning after 3 days when it fell into a lake near the city of ███████. Tests made with SCP-5181 reveal that it is made of a metal of unknown origin,

but almost twice the strength of steel and will not rust.

                    

                                    





            
    

                    



                    
                        
                            
